A signal that hands the turn back to the thread that paid for it, which pays for it still.
A turn's payer is the turn's own thread.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-rp2350 fuzz-smp2 fuzz-work qemu-replay
Report: a turn's payer is not another thread of its core

diff --git a/kernel/sched.c b/kernel/sched.c
--- a/kernel/sched.c
+++ b/kernel/sched.c
@@ -558,7 +558,6 @@ void sched_turn_back(void)
 {
     struct core *core = core_self();
     struct thread *was = core->turn, *payer = core->payer;
-    core->payer = NULL;
     core->turn = payer;
     thread_settle(was);
     thread_settle(payer);
